cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SEME: A Decoupled Evaluation Protocol for Literature-Constrained EEG–Drug Generators"
message: "If you use this software or protocol, please cite this manuscript, this repository, and the Zenodo checkpoint deposit."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Haris"
    given-names: "Muhammad"
    affiliation: "University of Wah"
abstract: >
  SEME (Signed concordance, Effect-vector fidelity, Magnitude transfer,
  Encoding retention) is an evaluation protocol for literature-constrained,
  chemistry-conditioned EEG generative models, demonstrated on a
  pharmacodynamically penalized Donepezil/Memantine CVAE case study.
keywords:
  - SEME
  - EEG
  - CVAE
  - evaluation protocol
  - pharmacodynamic constraints
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Muhammad-Haris123/eeg-seme-public"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-20"
identifiers:
